<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss bond market closing report.</title>
<headline>Swiss bond market closing report.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss bond prices ended higher on Wednesday before release of German and Swiss December unemployment data on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders expected the German data especially to be favourable for the market.</p>
<p>German data are due at 0900 GMT, and Swiss data are expected roughly a half hour before at about 0830 GMT.</p>
<p>Traders said the short end of the market was helped by the Swiss franc's steadier tone, while the longer end rose on short-covering after recent declines.  </p>
<p>-- Wednesday's closing prices as follows:</p>
<p>Mar Conf futures up 36 at 115.84.</p>
<p>Mar Comi medium-term bond up 20 at 111.00</p>
<p>Mar Euro Swiss francs up seven at 98.17.</p>
<p>4-1/2 Jun 2007 bond 104.35/45 yield 3.967</p>
<p>(Close on Tuesday 104.08/104.18 yld 3.999)</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
